<title>AUSTRALIA: Trade unions plan blockade of Western Australia.</title>
<headline>Trade unions plan blockade of Western Australia.</headline>
<dateline>MELBOURNE 1997-04-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Australian trade unions plan a communications and transport blockade of Western Australia on April 29 to protest against the state's proposed labour reforms, the Australian Council of Trade Unions (ACTU) said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>The ACTU said in a statement unions in the communications and transport sectors resolved at a meeting in Melbourne on Tuesday to blockade the huge resource-rich state for a day as part of a &quot;continuing campaign of action&quot;.</p>
</text>
